    <p class="rb-section-italic rb-section-italic--center">A note from us</p>
    <h2 class="rb-letter-head">
      There is a quality of attention that changes everything.
    </h2>

    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      When we stop performing, stop explaining, stop arranging ourselves
      for the room — and simply allow ourselves to be heard — something
      settles. Something true comes forward.
    </p>
    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      This is the work we do together at this retreat. Not big
      interventions. Not breakthroughs on demand. A returning, instead, to
      a more honest frequency. A way of being with each other that feels
      almost like an older, more indigenous way of knowing — where we
      listen below the story, find the places within ourselves that
      indicate truth, and trust what we find there.
    </p>
    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      When a circle holds that kind of attention, healing is not something
      we chase. It is simply <em>what happens.</em>
    </p>

    <p class="rb-letter-divider" aria-hidden="true">✦</p>

    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      This retreat is also built around one of the most ancient human
      technologies: the circle, the voice, the ritual of being part of
      something larger than ourselves.
    </p>
    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      Some of you are coming back. Some are coming for the first time.
      The work of these three days is to make a space where neither
      matters — where each person, whatever they bring, can drop into the
      circle and be received.
    </p>
    <p class="rb-letter-body">
      We will sound together. We will sit in silence together. We will
      share meals at one table. And in the centre of it all, we will craft
      a <em>ritual of belonging</em> — something none of us can make alone.
    </p>

    <p class="rb-letter-sig">— Lesanne &amp; Jacob</p>
  </div>
